{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/860231-chronicles-of-darkness-rules-or-old-wod-rules","id":860231,"title":"Chronicles of Darkness rules? or old WoD rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-06T04:55:11-07:00","id":860231,"title":"Chronicles of Darkness rules? or old WoD rules?","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I've recently bought the new Requiem book, and all the changes of rules were really nice! For what I've seen, all the new books are following the same pattern now: no need for the chronicles of darkness book (I guess it's the new World of Darkness rulebook), since all the rules are already explained in the proper book, and the improved rules (particularly giving a huge boost in power to the creatures in the dark).<br /> <br /> I know that the new Requiem and Forsaken follow these rules, and the new Awakening will be out soon. Does Demon also have these updated rules? Are they in the rulebook, or is it like Mummy, which still uses the old WoD rules and need the basic WoD book? Basically my question is: having read the new Requiem, can I expect a similarly organized book in Demon? In case it follows the old WoD rules, will it be updated soon to CoD? I think that the setting is interesting, but I really don't want to buy an already deprecated book...<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11574-andarea","name":"Andarea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:05:11-07:00","id":860239,"title":"","content":"Glad you're enjoying the second edition rules! Demon: the Descent was the second book released for the current edition, between the God-Machine Chronicle and the Requiem 2e core. Unfortunately, Requiem 2e was the first CofD monster corebook to use its layout format, with the standalone rules and the sample settings chapter and all. Demon is laid out like a 1e monster corebook, plus an appendix in the back that updates 1e core rules to 2e rules. Fortunately, since you already have Requiem providing the basic CofD 2e rules, you won't need to purchase multiple books to play Demon; rather than referencing the appendix and the core CofD rulebook, you can use the Requiem book to supply the general system, and Demon-specific rules all slot in comfortably into the 2e structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}